    "explanation": "Both of you: this case is decided on the trip's own measurements, and the rider's refund claim is not supported. The governing distance is gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 2.71 km (EV-GPS-00519) against an optimal_distance_km of 5.0 km (EV-TRIP-00519). The excess is therefore minus 2.29 km, i.e. -45.8%: the vehicle travelled LESS far than the platform's optimal route, not more. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds 20% of the optimal AND exceeds 0.8 km in absolute terms, and a negative excess passes neither limb. No route deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION 'however the rider characterises the trip'. The 9.99 charged (EV-FARE-00519, total_charged 9.99, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0) stands. Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative: on this rider-filed dispute it leaves the charge exactly as it is.\n\nTo the rider: EV-CHAT-00519 shows your instruction 'take Clementi Rd then North Buona Vista, fewer lights' sent at 08:08:10 and read at 08:08:35, and your follow-up 'hello?' at 08:10:40, with no reply; the driver's own statement confirms he declined to take your road. That is accepted as fact, but it does not change the outcome. POL-RD-04 governs a deviation attributable to a rider request, the converse of what happened here - there is no excess to attribute - and the message carries waypoint_hint null, so the clause's corroboration test cannot even be run. POL-RD-04 does not create a deviation or an entitlement on this trip. The failure to communicate is a genuine grievance, but it is not a route deviation and this category provides no monetary remedy for it. It also produces no referral: POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review fires only where a MATERIAL deviation is found and the driver profile shows a trailing-90-day pattern (deviation_flags_90d of 3 or more, or 0.05 or more of completed_trips_90d with at least 40 trips). There is no deviation at all here, and EV-DPROF-00519 records deviation_flags_90d of 0 across 250 completed trips in the window, so no conduct referral is generated.\n\nTo the driver: your account of the measurement is correct and forms the basis of the ruling.\n\nOn the fare arithmetic: even if POL-RD-02 were reached, recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 5.0 + 0.28 x 9.0) x surge multiplier 1.0 read from EV-FARE-00519) + 0.80 platform fee = 10.87, against a charged_total of 9.99. The refund would floor at zero, and the ledger's quantum of 0.05 is below the 0.50 de minimis. The rider was in fact charged less than the optimal-route metered fare.\n\nOn billing integrity (POL-RD-09(4)): EV-FARE-00519 itemises no ERP gantries (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00, optimal_route_erp 0.00) and no airport surcharge (0.00) on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport. Every charge line (base fare 3.80, distance 2.03, time 3.36, platform fee 0.80) has a counterpart in the trace or trip record. There is no phantom or unmatched line, so no billing-integrity refund or referral arises.\n\nNo escalation trigger fired. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (coverage_pct 100.0, gaps empty, max_gap_sec 0.0, point_count 73 at a 10 s cadence, weight 1.0), so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged; trip identifiers match across EV-TRIP-00519, EV-GPS-00519 and EV-FARE-00519; timestamps are consistent; and no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00519-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) was not relied on by either side, and no party asserts an external traffic cause, so there is nothing for POL-RD-03, POL-RD-10(5) or POL-RD-13 to test. The driver's shortfall argument (2.71 km trace versus 2.70 km trip-record copy) does not straddle any threshold; both are far below the 5.0 km optimal, and the trace figure governs under POL-RD-01 in any event.\n\nConfidence is 0.95. The deciding facts - the trace distance, the optimal distance and the absence of any unmatched charge - are carried by weight-1.0 artifacts (EV-GPS-00519, EV-TRIP-00519, EV-FARE-00519), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and the platform-wide 0.70 floor is comfortably cleared.",
